-- Owner requested removal of superseded kitchen concepts. Preserve unrelated notes and all other renovations.
DELETE FROM design_entries WHERE project='kitchen' AND kind IN ('favorite','render-request') AND json_extract(content,'$.concept') IN ('kitchen-extension','winter-full-west-view-v2','winter-full-north-view-v2');
UPDATE design_entries SET content=json_set(content,'$.text','Start from the confirmed A+B footprint traced on the original exposé inset: A is the long WEST wing alongside the existing kitchen; B is the shallower NORTH return; C is the existing kitchen; D is its EAST cooker wall. The owner confirmed this outline on 14 September 2026. Keep these proportions and orientation in every study. The approximately 40 m² reported in the exposé is not a measured area verification. Explore a year-round kitchen and dining room with expanded preparation and storage, generous glazing, timber and stone. Begin by comparing a freestanding west-wing dining table with a west-side banquette; the north return can be a sitting or reading edge. Keep the existing cooker wall and island as starting anchors. Test improvements to the existing kitchen working area. Do not assume large wall removals or a deep north dining room. Preserve source openings in initial layouts; any enlarged opening is a separate structural proposal. Verify furniture clearances, dimensions, roof and approved drawings before producing geometry-based interior views. The earlier kitchen images and their inferred layouts have been discarded.'),version=version+1,updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE project='kitchen' AND kind='brief' AND json_extract(content,'$.text')='Use the entire approximately 40 m² L-shaped wintergarten opportunity shown in the exposé, extending WEST alongside the kitchen and NORTH beyond it, with the two wings meeting at the north-west corner. The full footprint is the starting requirement. Create one fully heated, year-round kitchen and dining space. Expand functional cooking, preparation and storage space into the west wing and test a generous dining area in the north wing; keep the two wings visually and physically connected. Verify the final outline against the actual approved drawings. Use generous glazing, natural timber and stone. Explore retaining and adapting the existing kitchen and La Cornue range, as well as a more comprehensive reconfiguration. Maintain a strong connection to the original house and garden.';
